funcrunch wrote:
> I've been playing Nethack for over 14 years,

Mee too.

> and the number of hit
> points I feel the need for has steadily increased.

Not me. In my early days I felt comfortable with 300-360 maxHP's.
Recently I noticed that 120 maxHP's are not enough for me. So with
about 180-200 HP's I feel fine now.

Encounters with air elementals likely make it necessary, though, to
quaff full healing; which will increase the value of maxHP's displayed
on the ascension list whether you need the maxHP boost or not. Thus
Shawn's interesting numbers posted in this thread must be taken with
some care; one does not need that many HP's as shown in the table
(mine are reported to be around 240-250).

> [...] I like having that extra margin
> of safety to not even have to look at my HP on the ascension run.

I don't think this is to recommend (whereever the personally felt
"save margin" for maxHP's is); better always have a close look at your
actual HP's. It's not much effort that you need mostly in few selected
situations.

> But my latest Cavewoman didn't want to leave any kinds of potions of
> healing behind, alchemizing and quaffing all to a max of over 600HP,
> which seemed a bit ridiculous. I know, some players have gotten
> millions of HP in long games through polyself bug abuse or whatever,
> but that's not my goal or interest. Am I wasting my time gaining so
> many HP?

Not ridiculous, but definitely a waste of time. (But if one enjoys it
that way, why not? :-)

> Not that I'm going for a speed ascension, but could always
> stand to be more efficient. Blessed potions of full healing are
> quicker and more reliable than nurses/foocubi, but do involve carrying
> extra inventory around while collecting sufficient gain energy and
